KG42.register("rules-2aa43d25ee12f075da1b5b60",{"id":"04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R004","paper":"04-energy_collectives","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The within-community trading price enters each prosumer's individual cost-minimization objective through the term λ_c q_j, providing the local price input to coordination of decentralized participant decisions. Scope: Within-community trading in the energy-collective equilibrium formulation (18)–(20). Condition: The equilibrium formulation assumes perfect competition.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Within-community trading in the energy-collective equilibrium formulation (18)–(20).","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x-q_j","symbol":"q_j","meaning":"Community-level energy exchange of prosumer j (source nomenclature: energy imported by prosumer j from the community); the quantity multiplied by the within-community price λ_c in the prosumer objective term λ_c q_j.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued community exchange variable for prosumer j within Γ; subject to the per-prosumer balance p_j + q_j + α_j − β_j = 0 and the community balance Σ_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0 in the equilibrium formulation","unit":null,"indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_c","symbol":"λ_c","meaning":"Within-community trading price; in the equilibrium formulation (18)–(20), λ_c is the price for trading within the community and the multiplier associated with the internal market balance Σ_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0 under perfect competition.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"dual variable / within-community price signal associated with (20a); not assigned a numeric value in the supplied evidence"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The within-community trading price enters each prosumer's individual cost-minimization objective through the term λ_c q_j, providing the local price input to coordination of decentralized participant decisions. Scope: Within-community trading in the energy-collective equilibrium formulation (18)–(20). Condition: The equilibrium formulation assumes perfect competition.","expression":"\\lambda_c q_j \\quad \\text{(within-community price term in objective (18a))}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x-q_j"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_c"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"At optimality of the equilibrium problem (18)–(20), the within-community price λ_c appears in the stationarity condition for each prosumer's community exchange q_j: ∂h/∂q_j + π_j + λ_c = 0 for all j; this is the marginal counterpart of the objective term λ_c q_j.","expression":"\\frac{\\partial h}{\\partial q_j} + \\pi_j + \\lambda_c = 0 \\quad \\forall j \\quad (21b)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x-q_j"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_c"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E16"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Under the perfect-competition assumption of the equilibrium formulation, the internal community balance is Σ_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0 and λ_c is its associated multiplier, making λ_c the within-community trading price.","expression":"\\sum_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0 \\quad (\\lambda_c) \\quad (20a)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x-q_j"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_c"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E18","v141-b-g03-E16"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p10-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":10,"printed_page":"4003","section":"Appendix","anchor_text":"Γ i∈Ij + λcqj + λiαj −λeβj s.t. uij + qj + αj + βj = 0 (πj) (18b) i∈Ij uij −¯Uij ≤0 ∀i (γMij ) (18c)","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We then write the relative equilibrium problem, in which each prosumer j minimizes its costs following\nmin_{Γ} Σ_{i∈I_j} ψ_{ij}(u_{ij}) + h_j(q_j, α_j, β_j) + λ_c q_j + λ_i α_j − λ_e β_j   (18a)\ns.t.  Σ_{i∈I_j} u_{ij} + q_j + α_j + β_j = 0   (π_j)   (18b)\nu_{ij} − \\bar{U}_{ij} ≤ 0   ∀i   (γ^{M}_{ij})   (18c)\n\\underline{U}_{ij} − u_{ij} ≤ 0   ∀i   (γ^{m}_{ij})   (18d)\n− α_j ≤ 0   (γ^{a}_{j})   (18e)\n− β_j ≤ 0   (γ^{b}_{j})   (18f)\nwhere λ_c is the price for trading within the community and λ_i and λ_e respectively the price for buying and selling energy with the market operator."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p10-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":10,"printed_page":"4003","section":"Appendix","anchor_text":"Under the assumption of perfect competition, we can modeld) market constraints as n e) qj = 0 (λc) (","equation_id":"(20)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Under the assumption of perfect competition, we can model market constraints as\nΣ_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0   (λ_c)   (20a)\nΣ_{j=1}^{n} α_j − q_imp = 0   (λ_i)   (20b)\nΣ_{j=1}^{n} β_j − q_exp = 0   (λ_e)   (20c)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p01-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":"3994","section":"Abstract and Nomenclature","anchor_text":"Only the most important symbols of this paper are included. αj Energy imported by prosumer j. βj Ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Only the most important symbols of this paper are included. alpha_j Energy imported by prosumer j. beta_j Energy exported by prosumer j. delta_j Upper bound of alpha_j. gamma Penalization coefficient (the subscript identifies the specific application). lambda_j Price of energy perceived by prosumer j. lambda_DA Day-ahead market price. P_j Feasible space of p_j. R_j Feasible space of prosumer j. U_ij Feasible space of u_ij. U-upper_ij Upper bound of asset i of prosumer j. psi_ij Cost/utility function of asset i of prosumer j. rho Penalization factor of L_rho. tau Price spread between import and export price. f-tilde_j Extended cost function of prosumer j. U-lower_ij Lower bound of asset i of prosumer j. c_ij Quadratic coefficient of psi_ij. d_ij Linear coefficient of psi_ij. f_j Cost function of prosumer j. g Model of community manager. h_j Preferences and/or transaction costs of prosumer j. I_j Set of assets of prosumer j. L_rho Augmented Lagrangian. n Number of prosumers in the collective. N_j Set of members of neighbourhood j. p_j Net energy produced by prosumer j. q_j Energy imported by prosumer j from the community. q_exp Total energy exported. q_imp Total energy imported. r_k Vector of primal residuals. s_k Vector of dual residuals. u_ij Power set-point of asset i of prosumer j. v_ij Energy traded between neighbourhood i and j. y Vector of Lagrangian multipliers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-dfa28329fc-p10-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":10,"printed_page":"4003","section":"Appendix","anchor_text":"MORET AND PINSON: ENERGY COLLECTIVES: A COMMUNITY AND FAIRNESS BASE where the dual variables of each","equation_id":"(17)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"where the dual variables of each constraint are reported within brackets. The KKT conditions of (16) then become\nψ'_{ij}(u_{ij}) + π_j + γ^{M}_{ij} − γ^{m}_{ij} = 0   ∀i, j   (17a)\n∂h/∂q_j + π_j + λ_c = 0   ∀j   (17b)\n∂h/∂α_j + π_j + λ_i − γ^{a}_{j} = 0   ∀j   (17c)\n∂h/∂β_j + π_j + λ_e − γ^{b}_{j} = 0   ∀j   (17d)\n∂g/∂q_imp − λ_i − γ_i = 0   (17e)\n∂g/∂q_exp − λ_e − γ_e = 0   (17f)\nΣ_{i∈I_j} u_{ij} + q_j + α_j + β_j = 0   ∀j   (17g)\nΣ_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0   (17h)\nΣ_{j=1}^{n} α_j − q_imp = 0   (17i)\nΣ_{j=1}^{n} β_j − q_exp = 0   (17j)\n0 ≤ \\bar{U}_{ij} − u_{ij} ⊥ γ^{M}_{ij} ≥ 0   ∀i, j   (17k)\n0 ≤ u_{ij} − \\underline{U}_{ij} ⊥ γ^{m}_{ij} ≥ 0   ∀i, j   (17l)\n0 ≤ α_j ⊥ γ^{a}_{j} ≥ 0   ∀j   (17m)\n0 ≤ β_j ⊥ γ^{b}_{j} ≥ 0   ∀j   (17n)\n0 ≤ q_imp ⊥ γ_i ≥ 0   (17o)\n0 ≤ q_exp ⊥ γ_e ≥ 0   (17p)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E16","quote":"We then write the relative equilibrium problem, in which each prosumer j minimizes its costs following min_{Γ} Σ_{i∈I_j} ψ_{ij}(u_{ij}) + h_j(q_j, α_j, β_j) + λ_c q_j + λ_i α_j − λ_e β_j   (18a)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E16","quote":"where λ_c is the price for trading within the community"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","quote":"Under the assumption of perfect competition, we can model market constraints as Σ_{j=1}^{n} q_j = 0   (λ_c)   (20a)"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e095eb9d7d8bc3858d2f66e1eb9af9a78926706c63df9fc5f5774611e84ec2d3","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source equilibrium formulation explicitly contains the term λ_c q_j in each prosumer's individual objective (18a), with λ_c defined as the price for trading within the community; the same λ_c appears in the internal-balance multiplier (20a) and in the corresponding stationarity condition (21b). The frozen graph's nodes pricing.local and coordination.price_signal and edge v141-c-R004-E001 suffice to represent this price-signal relation. x is q_j, the operational community-exchange quantity, and theta is λ_c, the within-community price signal. C001's kind is updated from procedural to mathematical because a supported source expression is now present; its constraint_id, statement, role, members, and original evidence_ids are retained. B evidence remains unreviewed, and no claim is made that λ_c equals the separately printed λ_com from p.8.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-x-q_j","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"q_j is the community-exchange decision quantity that is multiplied by the local price λ_c in the price-signal term λ_c q_j. pricing.local supplies the local price and coordination.price_signal is the coordination relation through which that price enters the prosumer objective; edge E001 links pricing.local to coordination.price_signal under C001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_c","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"λ_c is the within-community trading price defined in E16 and associated with the internal balance (20a) in E18. It is the local price signal supplied by pricing.local and used in coordination.price_signal via the term λ_c q_j; edge E001 is the frozen link between these nodes."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C001 states that λ_c q_j enters the prosumer cost-minimization objective. pricing.local is the price source and coordination.price_signal is the coordination relation; edge E001 links them and carries C001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C002 is the source KKT stationarity condition (21b) showing the same local price λ_c in the marginal condition for q_j. It uses the same nodes and edge as the objective term, with λ_c from pricing.local entering coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C003 is the source internal-balance condition (20a) carrying multiplier λ_c, under the perfect-competition condition. It supports the identification of λ_c as the local price represented by pricing.local and used in coordination.price_signal; edge E001 links the two nodes."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
